On September 24, 2026, American International Group, Inc. (“AIG”) closed the sale of €625,000,000 aggregate principal amount of its 4.250% Notes Due 2031 (the “2031 Notes”) and €500,000,000 aggregate principal amount of its 4.750% Notes Due 2036 (the “2036 Notes” and, together with the 2031 Notes, the “Notes”).
The following documents relating to the sale of the Notes are filed as exhibits to this Current Report on Form 8-K and are incorporated into this Item 8.01 by reference:
• Underwriting Agreement, dated September 15, 2026, between AIG and Deutsche Bank AG, London Branch, J.P. Morgan Securities plc, BNP PARIBAS and Citigroup Global Markets Limited, as representatives of the several underwriters named in Schedule I thereto, relating to the Notes;
• Forty-Eighth Supplemental Indenture, dated September 24, 2026, between AIG and The Bank of New York Mellon, as Trustee, relating to the 2031 Notes;
• Forty-Ninth Supplemental Indenture, dated September 24, 2026, between AIG and The Bank of New York Mellon, as Trustee, relating to the 2036 Notes;
• Form of the 2031 Notes;
• Form of the 2036 Notes; and
• Opinion of Sullivan & Cromwell LLP, dated September 24, 2026, as to the validity of the Notes.
